		$d = json_decode( <<<'TFJSON'
[{"slug": "best-spa-in-ubud-guide", "title": "Best Spa in Ubud: How to Choose Your Treatment (2026 Guide)", "excerpt": "How to choose a spa in Ubud, what each treatment really does, what it costs and how to plan your visit around the rice fields and the jungle.", "html": "<p>Ubud is the wellness heart of Bali. Between the rice terraces, the yoga shalas and the jungle there are hundreds of spas, from five-dollar roadside massages to resort spas with a view. Choosing one is harder than it looks. This guide explains what really makes a good spa in Ubud, which treatments are worth it, what they cost and how to plan your visit so that you leave lighter, not more tired.</p>\n<h2>What makes a spa in Ubud worth your time</h2>\n<p>A good spa is not about marble or a big pool. It is about three things you can check before you book:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Trained therapists who specialise.</strong> A face massage and a body massage are different crafts. Ask who will treat you and how long they have worked with that technique.</li>\n<li><strong>A clear menu with real durations and prices.</strong> If the menu hides the price or the length of the treatment, you will be surprised at the end.</li>\n<li><strong>Time around the treatment.</strong> Tea, a quiet changing room and a few minutes of rest after the massage make the difference between a service and a ritual.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At <a href=\"/ubud/\">THE FACES Ubud</a>, in Kedewatan, close to Sanggingan, every treatment comes with that time. Anna and Evgenii Dubinin opened their first salon in Bali in 2013, and the team in Ubud follows the same method: specialised therapists, honest prices and no rush.</p>\n<h2>The treatments guests in Ubud choose most</h2>\n<h3>1. Full body massage</h3>\n<p>The classic for after a day of walking the Campuhan Ridge or the Tegallalang terraces. Our therapists combine Balinese pressure with long, calm strokes.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Full body massage, 60 min: IDR 650,000</li>\n<li>Full body massage, 90 min: IDR 900,000</li>\n<li>Full body massage, 120 min: IDR 950,000</li>\n<li>Fire Massage, 90 min: IDR 1,100,000, with warmth to release deep tension</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Read more on the <a href=\"/body-massage/\">body massage page</a>.</p>\n<h3>2. Face massage: the reason many guests find us</h3>\n<p>THE FACES started as a face studio, and face massage is still our signature. It is not a facial with creams: the therapist works with the muscles and the fascia of the face, the neck and the upper back.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Myofascial facial massage, 90 min: IDR 900,000, the most visible lift after one session</li>\n<li>Sculptural face massage, 90 min: IDR 850,000, a slower, holistic approach</li>\n<li>Buccal facial massage, 60 min: IDR 750,000, work from inside the cheeks for the jaw and contour</li>\n<li>Gua sha massage, 60 min: IDR 750,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Not sure which one? Our guide <a href=\"/face-massage/\">to face massage</a> compares them in detail.</p>\n<h3>3. Head spa</h3>\n<p>The treatment everyone is talking about in Bali. Warm water, scalp detox and a long head massage: many guests fall asleep in the first ten minutes. Try the Water spa therapy with detox hair spa (90 min, IDR 1,100,000) or the Shirodhara Hair Spa, with a warm oil stream on the forehead (120 min, IDR 1,650,000). In Ubud there is also Let Your Hair Shine (120 min, IDR 1,500,000) and a Hair spa for kids (60 min, IDR 750,000). See the <a href=\"/head-spa/\">head spa page</a>.</p>\n<h3>4. Five Elements rituals</h3>\n<p>Our three-hour programmes are built around Air, Fire, Water, Earth and Love. Each one combines several techniques, face, body and head, into one journey (180 min, IDR 1,800,000). They are the best choice if you have one afternoon and want the full THE FACES experience. Discover them on the <a href=\"/five-elements/\">Five Elements page</a>.</p>\n<h3>5. Treatments for men</h3>\n<p>Ubud has two programmes designed for men: Power Reset (130 min, IDR 1,400,000) and Stress Free (120 min, IDR 2,100,000).</p>\n<h2>How to plan your spa day in Ubud</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Book the afternoon or the evening.</strong> The morning is for the rice fields and the temples; the spa is the perfect end of the day. THE FACES Ubud is open until 22:00.</li>\n<li><strong>Arrive ten minutes early.</strong> You will have time for tea and to tell the therapist what you need.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not eat a heavy meal just before.</strong> A light lunch two hours before is ideal.</li>\n<li><strong>Keep an hour free after the treatment.</strong> Especially after a head spa or a ritual, give yourself time before you jump back on a scooter.</li>\n<li><strong>Tell us about pregnancy, injuries or allergies.</strong> The therapist will adapt the treatment or suggest another one.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Ubud or Sanur?</h2>\n<p>We have two salons. <a href=\"/ubud/\">Ubud</a> is surrounded by green and is open until 22:00, perfect if you stay in the centre or in Sayan and Kedewatan. <a href=\"/sanur/\">Sanur</a> is by the sea, quieter, and has a few treatments you will only find there, such as Hydrolift and the Sacred Honeymoon ritual. The full list is on our <a href=\"/menu/\">menu</a>.</p>\n<h2>Spa prices in Ubud: what you are paying for</h2>\n<p>Massage prices in Ubud range from very cheap street salons to resort spas that charge in dollars. The difference is not only the décor. A lower price usually means shorter real treatment time (a \"60-minute\" massage that starts late and finishes early), less training and oils of unknown origin. A higher price should buy you a specialised therapist, a full hour on the table, clean linen, quality products and a calm space. At THE FACES every price on the menu is the price you pay, the duration is the real time with your therapist, and tea and rest time are included.</p>\n<h2>Spa etiquette in Bali</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>What to wear:</strong> come as you are. We give you disposable underwear and a robe, and you are always covered with a towel.</li>\n<li><strong>Talking:</strong> tell the therapist if the pressure is too strong or too light, at any moment. After that, silence is welcome.</li>\n<li><strong>Tipping:</strong> it is not compulsory in Bali, but it is appreciated when you are happy with the treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>Arriving late:</strong> the treatment may have to be shortened so that the next guest is not delayed, so leave margin for Ubud traffic.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Which treatment for which day of your trip</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Arrival day, jet lag:</strong> a head spa or a Shirodhara Hair Spa to reset sleep.</li>\n<li><strong>After a volcano hike or a long scooter day:</strong> a 90-minute full body massage or the Fire Massage.</li>\n<li><strong>Before a wedding, a party or a photo shoot:</strong> a myofascial facial massage the day before.</li>\n<li><strong>Last day before flying:</strong> the Before Flight Ritual, which prepares the legs, head and face for the flight.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Book your treatment</h2>\n<p>You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a>, or write to the Ubud team on <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WhatsApp</a> and we will help you choose. Address: Jl. Raya Lungsiakan, Kedewatan, Ubud, Bali 80571. Open every day, 10:00–22:00.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">Face massage in Bali: which technique to choose</a></li><li><a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">Head spa in Bali: hair spa, Shirodhara and scalp detox</a></li><li><a href=\"/couples-spa-bali-honeymoon/\">Couples spa in Bali: rituals for two</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 7 min read", "img": "g06-interior.webp", "seo_title": "Best Spa in Ubud 2026: Treatments, Prices & How to Choose | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Looking for the best spa in Ubud? Face massage, head spa, Five Elements rituals and couples spa at THE FACES Ubud, open daily 10:00–22:00. Prices and tips.", "faq": [["What is the best spa treatment in Ubud for a first visit?", "For a first visit most guests choose a full body massage (60 or 90 minutes) or a Five Elements ritual. If you want a visible result on the face, choose the myofascial facial massage."], ["How much does a spa in Ubud cost?", "At THE FACES Ubud a 60-minute full body massage is IDR 650,000, face massages start at IDR 750,000 and the three-hour Five Elements rituals are IDR 1,800,000."], ["What are the opening hours of THE FACES Ubud?", "THE FACES Ubud is open every day from 10:00 to 22:00, so you can book a treatment after a day of sightseeing."], ["Do I need to book in advance?", "Yes, we recommend booking one or two days ahead, especially for evenings and for couples rituals. You can book online or on WhatsApp."]]}, {"slug": "head-spa-bali-guide", "title": "Head Spa in Bali: Hair Spa, Shirodhara and Scalp Detox Explained", "excerpt": "Everything about the head spa trend in Bali: what happens during a session, the benefits for the scalp and the nervous system, and which treatment to book.", "html": "<p>If you have scrolled Instagram or TikTok in Bali this year, you have seen it: a guest lying back, warm water falling over the scalp, foam, steam and a face that slowly relaxes. The head spa has become one of the most wanted treatments on the island. Here is what it really is, what happens during a session and how to choose the right one at THE FACES in Ubud or Sanur.</p>\n<h2>What is a head spa?</h2>\n<p>A head spa is a ritual for the scalp and the hair. It borrows from Japanese scalp care and from Ayurveda and combines four steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Diagnosis and cleansing.</strong> The therapist looks at the scalp and gently removes the build-up of sweat, sunscreen, salt water and styling products.</li>\n<li><strong>Warm water therapy.</strong> A slow stream of warm water relaxes the scalp and the nervous system.</li>\n<li><strong>Massage.</strong> Head, neck and shoulders, where most of us hold our tension.</li>\n<li><strong>Nourishing care.</strong> A mask or oil adapted to your hair, then a gentle dry.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The result: a light head, soft hair and a deep feeling of calm that many guests compare to a long night of sleep.</p>\n<h2>Why a head spa makes sense in Bali</h2>\n<p>Sun, humidity, salt water, chlorine and daily sunscreen are hard on the scalp. Many travellers notice dry lengths and an oily or itchy scalp after a few weeks on the island. A head spa resets both. It is also a perfect treatment for jet lag and for the last day before a long flight.</p>\n<h2>Head spa treatments at THE FACES</h2>\n<h3>Ayurvedic head massage · 60 min · IDR 750,000</h3>\n<p>The short version: a deep massage of the head, neck and shoulders with warm oil, inspired by Indian tradition. Ideal if you have an hour and want to switch off.</p>\n<h3>Water spa therapy with detox hair spa · 90 min · IDR 1,100,000</h3>\n<p>Our most booked head spa. Detox cleansing, a long warm water ritual and a massage that reaches the neck and shoulders. Perfect for a first head spa.</p>\n<h3>Shirodhara Hair Spa · 120 min · IDR 1,650,000</h3>\n<p>The deepest of all. A thin, continuous stream of warm oil flows over the forehead, the \"third eye\" in Ayurveda, while the hair receives a full spa. It is the treatment we recommend for stress, poor sleep and an overloaded mind.</p>\n<h3>Let Your Hair Shine · 120 min · IDR 1,500,000 · Ubud</h3>\n<p>Focused on the beauty of the hair: nourishing care for lengths damaged by sun and sea, with a relaxing head massage.</p>\n<h3>Hair spa for kids · 60 min · IDR 750,000 · Ubud</h3>\n<p>A gentle, playful version for children, so that the whole family can enjoy the spa.</p>\n<h2>Head spa combined with face massage</h2>\n<p>The combination of head spa and face massage is our favourite: the scalp and the face are connected by the same fascia, so working on both doubles the effect.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hair spa &amp; water detox + face massage, 120 min: IDR 1,500,000</li>\n<li>3 in 1 (head, face massage, hair spa): IDR 1,900,000</li>\n<li>Detox hair spa + myofascial facial massage, 150 min: IDR 1,850,000 (Sanur)</li>\n<li>Detox hair spa + sculptural face massage, 180 min: IDR 1,850,000 (Sanur)</li>\n<li>Water spa therapy with detox hair spa + Airkiss Detox Ritual, 120 min: IDR 1,900,000</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to choose your head spa</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>First time, one afternoon:</strong> Water spa therapy with detox hair spa.</li>\n<li><strong>Stress, insomnia, jet lag:</strong> Shirodhara Hair Spa.</li>\n<li><strong>Short on time:</strong> Ayurvedic head massage.</li>\n<li><strong>You want to look rested for an event or photos:</strong> a head spa + face massage combination.</li>\n<li><strong>Before a long flight:</strong> our Before Flight Ritual (IDR 2,200,000), which includes care for the head, face and legs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Tips before and after your head spa</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Come with your hair as it is: no need to wash it before.</li>\n<li>Plan no swimming pool or sea for the rest of the day, so the care can work.</li>\n<li>Drink water after the treatment and keep the evening calm.</li>\n<li>Tell the therapist if you have a sensitive scalp or a recent colour.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Head spa or a simple hair wash at the salon?</h2>\n<p>A hair wash takes five minutes and cleans the hair. A head spa takes one to two hours and treats the scalp, the skin where the hair grows, and the nervous system. The water is warm and slow, the massage is long and reaches the neck and shoulders, and the care is chosen for your scalp. It is closer to a massage than to a hairdresser visit.</p>\n<h2>The benefits guests feel most</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Deep relaxation:</strong> most guests feel calm within minutes, and many fall asleep.</li>\n<li><strong>Better sleep</strong> the following night, especially after Shirodhara.</li>\n<li><strong>Less tension</strong> in the forehead, the jaw, the neck and the shoulders.</li>\n<li><strong>A fresh scalp:</strong> sunscreen, sweat and salt are gently removed.</li>\n<li><strong>Soft, shiny hair</strong> after days of sun, sea and humidity.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How often should you do a head spa?</h2>\n<p>As a treat on holiday, one session is enough to feel the difference. If you live in Bali, a head spa every two to four weeks keeps the scalp balanced in the tropical climate. Guests with a lot of stress often book the Shirodhara Hair Spa once a month as their reset ritual.</p>\n<h2>Who should talk to us first</h2>\n<p>Tell the team before booking if you are pregnant, have a skin condition on the scalp, a very recent hair colour or treatment, or high blood pressure. The therapist will adapt the temperature, the oils and the pressure, or suggest another treatment.</p>\n<h2>Book your head spa</h2>\n<p>All the details are on the <a href=\"/head-spa/\">head spa page</a> and in the <a href=\"/menu/\">full menu</a>. You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/shirodhara-bali-ayurveda/\">Shirodhara in Bali: the Ayurvedic oil ritual</a></li><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "head", "cat": "Head spa · 7 min read", "img": "g10-proc-s.webp", "seo_title": "Head Spa Bali: Hair Spa, Shirodhara & Scalp Detox Prices | THE FACES", "metadesc": "What is a head spa and which one to choose in Bali? Water spa with detox hair spa, Shirodhara and Ayurvedic head massage in Ubud and Sanur, with prices.", "faq": [["What is a head spa?", "A head spa is a treatment for the scalp and the hair that combines cleansing, warm water, massage of the head, neck and shoulders and nourishing care. It relaxes deeply and leaves the hair soft and light."], ["How long does a head spa take?", "At THE FACES a head spa lasts from 60 minutes (Ayurvedic head massage) to 120 minutes (Shirodhara Hair Spa), and up to 180 minutes when combined with a face massage."], ["How much is a head spa in Bali?", "At THE FACES prices start at IDR 750,000 for the Ayurvedic head massage. The Water spa therapy with detox hair spa is IDR 1,100,000 and the Shirodhara Hair Spa is IDR 1,650,000."], ["Is head spa good for hair loss?", "A head spa improves the condition of the scalp and the circulation and helps you relax, which many people with stressed hair appreciate. It is not a medical treatment: for hair loss, consult a dermatologist."]]}, {"slug": "face-massage-bali-guide", "title": "Face Massage in Bali: Myofascial, Sculptural, Buccal or Gua Sha?", "excerpt": "A complete comparison of the face massages at THE FACES: how they work, who they are for, how many sessions you need and what they cost.", "html": "<p>Face massage is where THE FACES began, and it is still the treatment our guests travel across Bali for. It is not a classic facial with creams and steam: it is a manual technique that works with the muscles, the fascia and the lymph of the face. The result is visible: a lifted contour, a relaxed jaw, brighter skin and a face that looks rested. Here is how to choose between our techniques.</p>\n<h2>Why face massage works</h2>\n<p>We use more than forty muscles of the face every day: to speak, chew, frown at the screen and squint in the sun. Over time they become tense and the fascia, the thin tissue that wraps them, loses its elasticity. The face looks tired and the contour drops. A professional face massage releases that tension, improves circulation and lymphatic drainage and gives the face its natural shape back.</p>\n<h2>The four main techniques</h2>\n<h3>Myofascial facial massage · 90 min · IDR 900,000</h3>\n<p>The therapist works deep in the fascia of the face and continues to the neck, the décolleté and the upper back, where many face problems start. Tension in the jaw and the forehead melts, the oval looks lifted and the skin brighter.</p>\n<p><strong>For whom:</strong> you clench your teeth, work at a screen, want a visible lift after one visit.</p>\n<h3>Sculptural face massage · 90 min · IDR 850,000</h3>\n<p>It combines French osteopathic methods with natural rejuvenation techniques and works with the whole body, not only the face. It is slower and more holistic, and the contour changes gradually over a course.</p>\n<p><strong>For whom:</strong> long-term well-ageing, guests who want a deep, calm treatment.</p>\n<h3>Buccal facial massage · 60 min · IDR 750,000</h3>\n<p>Part of the massage is done from inside the mouth, with gloves, to reach the deep muscles of the cheeks and the jaw that cannot be reached from outside. It is intense and very effective for the lower face.</p>\n<p><strong>For whom:</strong> jaw tension, asymmetry, a softer lower contour.</p>\n<h3>Gua sha massage · 60 min · IDR 750,000</h3>\n<p>A traditional Chinese technique with a smooth stone tool. It drains, de-puffs and leaves the skin glowing.</p>\n<p><strong>For whom:</strong> puffiness, morning swelling, a quick glow before an evening out.</p>\n<h2>Our signature face massages</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Signature massage «The FACES», 90 min: IDR 900,000, the best of our techniques in one session</li>\n<li>Signature massage «Element of Love», 90 min: IDR 900,000</li>\n<li>Signature massage «Author», 90 min: IDR 850,000</li>\n<li>Signature technique: Air Kiss Sculpt &amp; Detox, 120 min: IDR 1,800,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In Sanur you can also book Hydrolift (60 min, IDR 850,000), Hydrolift + face massage (90 min, IDR 1,100,000) and 4 hands, a face massage with foot reflexology at the same time (IDR 950,000).</p>\n<h2>Quick comparison</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>Duration</th><th>Price (IDR)</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Myofascial</td><td>90 min</td><td>900,000</td><td>Visible lift, jaw tension</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sculptural</td><td>90 min</td><td>850,000</td><td>Long-term contour</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Buccal</td><td>60 min</td><td>750,000</td><td>Cheeks and jaw</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Gua sha</td><td>60 min</td><td>750,000</td><td>Puffiness, glow</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>How many sessions?</h2>\n<p>After one session the face already looks fresher and lifted. For a result that lasts, we recommend a course of five or six sessions, every three days, which fits perfectly into a two-week holiday in Bali.</p>\n<h2>Combine it with skin care or head spa</h2>\n<p>Face massage works even better on clean, hydrated skin. Combine it with a cleansing or Deep skin hydration (80 min, IDR 1,000,000) from our <a href=\"/skin-care/\">skin care menu</a>, or with a head spa: see our <a href=\"/head-spa/\">head spa guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Before and after</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Come without make-up if you can, or we will remove it.</li>\n<li>Avoid strong sun for the rest of the day.</li>\n<li>Drink water: massage stimulates lymphatic drainage.</li>\n<li>Tell us about recent injections, fillers or skin procedures: the therapist will adapt the technique.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Face massage or facial: what is the difference?</h2>\n<p>A facial works mainly on the skin: cleansing, exfoliation, masks and serums. A face massage works deeper, on the muscles, the fascia and the lymph under the skin. That is why a face massage changes the shape and the expression of the face, while a facial changes its surface. The two work beautifully together: a <a href=\"/skin-care/\">skin treatment</a> for the surface, a face massage for the contour.</p>\n<h2>What results to expect, and when</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Right after the session:</strong> a relaxed face, brighter skin, less puffiness and a more open look.</li>\n<li><strong>The next morning:</strong> the contour looks more defined and the face rested.</li>\n<li><strong>After a course of five or six sessions:</strong> the effect lasts longer, the jaw stays relaxed and the oval is firmer.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Who should avoid a face massage or ask us first</h2>\n<p>Postpone the treatment if you have an active skin infection, a fresh sunburn, a fever or a recent facial procedure. If you have had injections or fillers in the last weeks, tell the therapist: she will choose gentle techniques and avoid the treated areas. For buccal massage, tell us about any dental treatment in progress.</p>\n<h2>A face massage routine for your holiday</h2>\n<p>Many of our guests book a short course during their stay: a myofascial or sculptural massage on day one, a gua sha or buccal session a few days later, and a signature massage before flying home. Between sessions, drink plenty of water, protect your face from the midday sun and sleep on your back if you can.</p>\n<h2>Book your face massage</h2>\n<p>More details on the <a href=\"/face-massage/\">face massage page</a>. You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or ask us on WhatsApp which technique suits you: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/facial-bali-skin-care-guide/\">Facial in Bali: the complete skin care guide</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li><li><a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">Head spa in Bali: hair spa, Shirodhara and scalp detox</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "face", "cat": "Face · 8 min read", "img": "g01-face.webp", "seo_title": "Face Massage Bali: Myofascial, Buccal, Sculptural & Gua Sha | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Which face massage to choose in Bali? Myofascial, sculptural, buccal and gua sha compared: what each one does, results, duration and prices at THE FACES.", "faq": [["Which face massage gives the most visible lift?", "The myofascial facial massage gives the most visible lift after one session, because it releases the fascia of the face, the neck and the upper back."], ["How many face massage sessions do I need?", "One session already shows a fresher, lifted face. For a lasting effect we recommend a course of five or six sessions, every three days."], ["How much is a face massage at THE FACES?", "Face massages cost IDR 750,000 (buccal or gua sha, 60 min), IDR 850,000 (sculptural, 90 min) and IDR 900,000 (myofascial or signature, 90 min)."], ["Is face massage suitable before a wedding or photos?", "Yes. Book it one or two days before: the face looks rested and the contour more defined. Avoid strong techniques for the first time on the day itself."]]}, {"slug": "spa-in-sanur-guide", "title": "Spa in Sanur: Treatments, Prices and Tips for a Perfect Spa Day", "excerpt": "A complete guide to THE FACES Sanur: the treatments you can only find here, prices, how to combine them and how to plan a slow spa day by the sea.", "html": "<p>Sanur is the calm side of Bali: a long beach path, sunrise over the sea, families and slow mornings. It is also a wonderful place for a spa day, especially at the start or at the end of a trip, because the airport is close. Our salon <a href=\"/sanur/\">THE FACES Sanur</a> is on Jl. Danau Buyan, a few minutes from the beach. Here is everything you need to plan your visit.</p>\n<h2>Why choose a spa in Sanur</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Calm.</strong> Less traffic and noise than in Seminyak or Canggu.</li>\n<li><strong>Close to the airport.</strong> Perfect for a treatment on arrival or before a night flight.</li>\n<li><strong>Sea and spa in one day.</strong> Swim in the morning, spa in the afternoon, dinner by the beach.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Treatments you will only find in Sanur</h2>\n<h3>Hydrolift · 60 min · IDR 850,000</h3>\n<p>Intensive hydration and a lifting effect for skin tired by sun and air conditioning. Combine it with a face massage: Hydrolift + face massage, 90 min, IDR 1,100,000.</p>\n<h3>4 hands · IDR 950,000</h3>\n<p>Two therapists at the same time: a face massage and a foot reflexology. One of the most relaxing experiences on our menu.</p>\n<h3>Aqua Glow Ritual · 100 min · IDR 800,000</h3>\n<p>A body ritual focused on hydration and glow, perfect after days of sun and sea.</p>\n<h3>Sacred Honeymoon ritual · 200 min · IDR 3,800,000</h3>\n<p>Our longest ritual for two, created for honeymoons and anniversaries. Read our <a href=\"/couples-spa/\">couples spa guide</a>.</p>\n<h3>Head spa and face massage in one session</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Detox hair spa + myofascial facial massage, 150 min: IDR 1,850,000</li>\n<li>Detox hair spa + sculptural face massage, 180 min: IDR 1,850,000</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>The favourites of our Sanur guests</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Airkiss Detox Ritual</strong>, 60 min: IDR 1,300,000 in Sanur. Our airy foam ritual, light and deeply relaxing.</li>\n<li><strong>Foamy Dream Ritual</strong>, 120 min: IDR 2,300,000. A cloud of foam for the whole body.</li>\n<li><strong>Full body massage</strong>, 90 min: IDR 850,000 in Sanur.</li>\n<li><strong>Reflexology foot massage</strong>, 30 / 60 / 90 min: IDR 300,000 / 500,000 / 600,000. Ideal after walking the beach path.</li>\n<li><strong>Myofascial facial massage</strong>, 90 min: IDR 900,000. Our signature face massage.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>A perfect slow spa day in Sanur</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Sunrise on the beach</strong>, around 6:00, then breakfast.</li>\n<li><strong>A swim and a walk</strong> on the beach path in the morning.</li>\n<li><strong>Light lunch</strong> at least two hours before your treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>Spa in the afternoon</strong>: a head spa + face massage combination or a Foamy Dream Ritual.</li>\n<li><strong>Dinner by the sea</strong> and an early night.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The Before Flight Ritual</h2>\n<p>Flying home tonight? Our Before Flight Ritual (IDR 2,200,000, about three hours in Sanur) prepares the body for a long flight: care for the head, face and legs, so that you board relaxed and land less swollen. Book it for the afternoon of your departure day, and keep your luggage in the car.</p>\n<h2>Prices at a glance</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Treatment</th><th>Duration</th><th>Price (IDR)</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Full body massage</td><td>90 min</td><td>850,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Myofascial facial massage</td><td>90 min</td><td>900,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Hydrolift</td><td>60 min</td><td>850,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Airkiss Detox Ritual</td><td>60 min</td><td>1,300,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Foamy Dream Ritual</td><td>120 min</td><td>2,300,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Before Flight Ritual</td><td>about 180 min</td><td>2,200,000</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The full list is in our <a href=\"/menu/\">menu</a>.</p>\n<h2>Getting to THE FACES Sanur</h2>\n<p>The salon is on Jl. Danau Buyan, in the quiet residential part of Sanur, a few minutes by car or scooter from the beach path. From Ngurah Rai airport the drive usually takes around 30 minutes, depending on traffic, which is why so many guests come straight from or to the airport. Grab and Gojek drivers know the address, and there is space to park a scooter in front.</p>\n<h2>Sanur or Seminyak for a spa?</h2>\n<p>Seminyak and Canggu are lively, with beach clubs, traffic and noise. Sanur is the opposite: families, long-stay guests, early mornings and a slower pace. If you want a spa where you hear birds instead of motorbikes, and where you can walk out and still feel the calm, Sanur is the better choice.</p>\n<h2>A spa for the whole family</h2>\n<p>Sanur is a family destination, and our menu works for every member: face massages and rituals for parents, reflexology and leg massages for grandparents tired after the flight, and relaxing head care. Book side by side treatments so that everyone finishes at the same time.</p>\n<h2>Tips for your visit</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Book one or two days ahead, especially for the afternoon and for the 4 hands treatment, which needs two therapists.</li>\n<li>If you come straight from the beach, rinse off the salt and sand first and leave ten extra minutes.</li>\n<li>After a Hydrolift or a face massage, protect your face from strong sun for the rest of the day.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Book in Sanur</h2>\n<p>Address: Jl. Danau Buyan No. 34a, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Bali 80227. Open every day, 10:00–20:00. You can <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a> or write to the Sanur team on <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WhatsApp</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/things-to-do-in-sanur/\">Things to do in Sanur: a slow guide</a></li><li><a href=\"/couples-spa-bali-honeymoon/\">Couples spa in Bali: rituals for two</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li><li><a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">Face massage in Bali: which technique to choose</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 7 min read", "img": "g07-interior-s.webp", "seo_title": "Spa in Sanur Bali: Treatments, Prices & Spa Day Tips | THE FACES Sanur", "metadesc": "Planning a spa in Sanur? THE FACES Sanur on Jl. Danau Buyan: face massage, Hydrolift, head spa, Airkiss and honeymoon rituals. Open 10:00–20:00. Prices inside.", "faq": [["Where is THE FACES Sanur?", "THE FACES Sanur is at Jl. Danau Buyan No. 34a, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Bali 80227, a few minutes from the beach."], ["What are the opening hours in Sanur?", "THE FACES Sanur is open every day from 10:00 to 20:00."], ["Which treatments are only available in Sanur?", "Hydrolift, Hydrolift + face massage, 4 hands (face massage + foot reflexology), the Aqua Glow Ritual, the Sacred Honeymoon ritual and the detox hair spa combined with a myofascial or sculptural face massage."], ["Is Sanur a good place for a spa day?", "Yes. Sanur is calm, close to the airport and to the sea, so it is ideal for a slow spa day or for the last day before your flight."]]}, {"slug": "couples-spa-bali-honeymoon", "title": "Couples Spa in Bali: Honeymoon and Romantic Rituals for Two", "excerpt": "How to choose a couples spa in Bali, what happens during our rituals for two, prices and ideas to make your honeymoon or anniversary unforgettable.", "html": "<p>Bali is one of the most romantic places on Earth, and a spa ritual for two is one of the moments couples remember most from their trip. Whether it is your honeymoon, an anniversary or simply time together away from the screens, here is how to choose a couples spa in Bali and what to expect from our rituals at THE FACES in Ubud and Sanur.</p>\n<h2>What makes a good couples spa</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>One room, two therapists, the same rhythm.</strong> You start and finish together, so the experience is shared, not parallel.</li>\n<li><strong>Enough time.</strong> A real ritual for two lasts at least two and a half hours, with a welcome, the treatment and time to rest together.</li>\n<li><strong>A story.</strong> The best rituals are not just two massages: they have a beginning, a heart and a closing moment.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Our rituals for two</h2>\n<h3>Element of Love for a couple · 180 min · IDR 3,200,000</h3>\n<p>Inspired by the fifth of our <a href=\"/five-elements/\">Five Elements</a>, Love. A three-hour journey that combines body, face and head care, side by side. It is our most chosen ritual for anniversaries.</p>\n<h3>Sacred Eternal Love ritual · 175 min · IDR 3,300,000</h3>\n<p>A ritual built around connection and presence, with warm oils, slow massage and a closing moment for the two of you. Perfect for a proposal trip or a vow renewal.</p>\n<h3>Sacred Honeymoon ritual · 200 min · IDR 3,800,000 · Sanur</h3>\n<p>Our longest ritual, created for honeymooners. More than three hours of care for two, in our calm salon by the sea in <a href=\"/sanur/\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>More ideas for two</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Book the same treatment at the same time:</strong> for example two Airkiss Detox Rituals (IDR 1,200,000 each in Ubud, IDR 1,300,000 in Sanur) or two Foamy Dream Rituals (IDR 2,300,000 each).</li>\n<li><strong>One head spa, one face massage:</strong> if you have different needs, book side by side treatments of the same length.</li>\n<li><strong>Five Elements for two:</strong> each partner chooses their element (180 min, IDR 1,800,000 per person).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Ubud or Sanur for a couples spa?</h2>\n<p><a href=\"/ubud/\">Ubud</a> is the jungle and the rice fields, and our salon is open until 22:00, ideal for an evening ritual after a day of exploring. <a href=\"/sanur/\">Sanur</a> is the sea and calm, and the only place to book the Sacred Honeymoon ritual. Many couples split their stay: a few nights in Ubud, a few by the sea.</p>\n<h2>How to make it unforgettable</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Book in advance</strong>: two or three days, as two therapists are needed at the same time.</li>\n<li><strong>Tell us the occasion</strong> when you book: honeymoon, anniversary, birthday. We love preparing small surprises.</li>\n<li><strong>Plan nothing after</strong>: no scooter rides or busy dinners. Go for a quiet dinner and an early night.</li>\n<li><strong>Leave the phones</strong> in the changing room. The ritual starts when the screens go off.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Prices for two at a glance</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Ritual</th><th>Duration</th><th>Price for two (IDR)</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Element of Love for a couple</td><td>180 min</td><td>3,200,000</td><td>Ubud &amp; Sanur</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sacred Eternal Love ritual</td><td>175 min</td><td>3,300,000</td><td>Ubud &amp; Sanur</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sacred Honeymoon ritual</td><td>200 min</td><td>3,800,000</td><td>Sanur</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>A three-day honeymoon itinerary with spa</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Day 1, Ubud:</strong> sunrise at the rice terraces, lunch in the jungle, and an evening Element of Love ritual for a couple at THE FACES Ubud, open until 22:00.</li>\n<li><strong>Day 2, between Ubud and the coast:</strong> temples in the morning, the drive to the sea in the afternoon, a slow dinner on the beach.</li>\n<li><strong>Day 3, Sanur:</strong> swim at sunrise, then the Sacred Honeymoon ritual in the afternoon, more than three hours just for the two of you.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>A spa ritual as a gift</h2>\n<p>Looking for a surprise for your partner? A couples ritual is one of the most meaningful gifts in Bali: time together, care and a memory you will both keep. Book it under your name, tell us it is a surprise, and we will keep the secret until you arrive.</p>\n<h2>What to expect on the day</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Welcome:</strong> tea and a few minutes to tell the therapists your preferences: pressure, areas to avoid, the occasion.</li>\n<li><strong>The ritual:</strong> you are treated side by side in the same room, by two therapists working in the same rhythm.</li>\n<li><strong>Closing:</strong> time to rest together before you leave, without rushing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Good to know</h2>\n<p>Tell us when you book if one of you is pregnant, has an injury or an allergy to oils: each ritual can be adapted. If one partner prefers a lighter treatment, the therapists will adjust the pressure for each person while keeping the same rhythm.</p>\n<h2>Book your couples ritual</h2>\n<p>All the details are on the <a href=\"/couples-spa/\">couples spa page</a>. You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp and tell us the occasion: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/things-to-do-in-sanur/\">Things to do in Sanur</a></li><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 7 min read", "img": "g08-interior.webp", "seo_title": "Couples Spa Bali: Honeymoon & Romantic Spa Rituals | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Best couples spa in Bali for a honeymoon or anniversary: Element of Love for a couple, Sacred Eternal Love and Sacred Honeymoon rituals in Ubud and Sanur.", "faq": [["What is the best couples spa treatment in Bali?", "At THE FACES we offer three rituals for two: Element of Love for a couple (180 min), the Sacred Eternal Love ritual (175 min) and the Sacred Honeymoon ritual (200 min, Sanur)."], ["How much is a couples spa in Bali?", "Our couples rituals cost IDR 3,200,000 (Element of Love for a couple), IDR 3,300,000 (Sacred Eternal Love) and IDR 3,800,000 (Sacred Honeymoon) for two people."], ["Can we have treatments side by side?", "Yes, our couples rituals are designed for two people at the same time in the same room."], ["Should we book a couples spa in advance?", "Yes. Couples rituals need two therapists at the same time, so we recommend booking two or three days ahead, especially for weekends and evenings."]]}, {"slug": "massage-in-ubud-guide", "title": "Massage in Ubud: Types, Prices and How to Choose (2026)", "excerpt": "A practical guide to massage in Ubud: the main types, what each one does, honest prices, how long to book and how to recognise a good therapist.", "html": "<p>Massage is part of daily life in Ubud. You will find it in tiny family studios, in yoga retreats and in luxury resorts, at prices that go from a few dollars to a few hundred. That choice is wonderful, but it also makes it easy to end up with a rushed, forgettable treatment. This guide explains the main types of massage you will find in Ubud, what each one is good for, what a fair price looks like and how to choose the right one for your body and your day.</p>\n<h2>Why Ubud is the best place in Bali for a massage</h2>\n<p>Ubud has been the island's centre of healing arts for generations. Many Balinese families have passed massage techniques from parents to children, and the town now attracts therapists trained in Ayurveda, Chinese medicine, osteopathy and modern sports massage. Add the calm of the rice fields and the jungle, and you have the perfect setting to slow down. The challenge is not finding a massage, it is finding a good one.</p>\n<h2>The main types of massage in Ubud</h2>\n<h3>Balinese massage</h3>\n<p>The traditional massage of the island combines firm palm and thumb pressure, gentle stretches and long strokes with warm oil. It releases tension and improves circulation. In our salon the Balinese technique is the base of the full body massage.</p>\n<h3>Full body massage</h3>\n<p>The classic choice: back, legs, arms, neck and shoulders, with pressure adapted to you. At THE FACES Ubud:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>60 min: IDR 650,000</li>\n<li>90 min: IDR 900,000</li>\n<li>120 min: IDR 950,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If it is your first massage in Bali, choose 90 minutes: it gives the therapist time to work on the areas that really need it.</p>\n<h3>Fire Massage · 90 min · IDR 1,100,000</h3>\n<p>Our warming massage for deep tension. Heat relaxes the muscles so that the therapist can work deeper without pain. Perfect after a Mount Batur sunrise hike, a surf lesson or days on a scooter.</p>\n<h3>Foot reflexology</h3>\n<p>Pressure on precise points of the feet, linked in reflexology to the whole body. It is deeply relaxing and ideal after walking the Campuhan Ridge or the Monkey Forest.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>30 min: IDR 300,000</li>\n<li>60 min: IDR 500,000</li>\n<li>90 min: IDR 600,000</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Lymphatic drainage / relaxing leg massage</h3>\n<p>Light, rhythmic movements that help the body release excess fluid. The best treatment for heavy, swollen legs after a long flight or hot days. 30 min IDR 300,000, 60 min IDR 500,000, 90 min IDR 600,000. Read our full guide to <a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">lymphatic drainage in Bali</a>.</p>\n<h3>Face massage</h3>\n<p>THE FACES is best known for face massage: myofascial (90 min, IDR 900,000), sculptural (90 min, IDR 850,000), buccal and gua sha (60 min, IDR 750,000). They lift and relax the face in a way no facial can. See our <a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">face massage guide</a>.</p>\n<h3>Head massage and head spa</h3>\n<p>The Ayurvedic head massage (60 min, IDR 750,000) and our head spa treatments with warm water are perfect for stress and poor sleep. Everything is explained in our <a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">head spa guide</a>.</p>\n<h3>Foam massage and Airkiss</h3>\n<p>Our signature foam rituals are unique in Ubud: the Airkiss Detox Ritual (60 min, IDR 1,200,000), the Foamy back &amp; leg massage (60 min, IDR 1,400,000) and the Foamy Dream Ritual (120 min, IDR 2,300,000), in which the body is wrapped in a warm cloud of foam.</p>\n<h2>Which massage for which situation?</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Our recommendation</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>First massage in Bali</td><td>Full body massage, 90 min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>After Mount Batur or a long hike</td><td>Fire Massage + reflexology 30 min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Jet lag, poor sleep</td><td>Ayurvedic head massage or Shirodhara Hair Spa</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Swollen legs after the flight</td><td>Lymphatic drainage leg massage, 60 min</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tired face, jaw tension</td><td>Myofascial facial massage</td></tr>\n<tr><td>A special treat</td><td>Foamy Dream Ritual or a Five Elements ritual</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>How to recognise a good massage in Ubud</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The therapist asks questions before starting:</strong> pressure, injuries, areas to avoid.</li>\n<li><strong>The duration is real:</strong> 60 minutes on the table, not 60 minutes including the time to change.</li>\n<li><strong>Clean linen and quality oil:</strong> you should not smell old oil or see stained towels.</li>\n<li><strong>A quiet room:</strong> no loud music from the street, no therapists chatting.</li>\n<li><strong>No pressure to buy:</strong> a good spa recommends, it does not push packages.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Massage prices in Ubud explained</h2>\n<p>Very cheap massages exist in Ubud, and some are good. But a price that is too low usually means less time, less training or tired therapists working long shifts. In a professional spa you pay for a specialised therapist, a calm room, clean linen, quality products and time before and after the treatment. At THE FACES the price on the <a href=\"/menu/\">menu</a> is the final price and the duration is the real time with your therapist.</p>\n<h2>Practical tips</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Book ahead</strong> for the evening: 17:00–21:00 is the busiest time in Ubud.</li>\n<li><strong>Leave margin for traffic:</strong> the roads around Ubud centre are slow in the late afternoon.</li>\n<li><strong>Eat lightly before</strong> and drink water after the massage.</li>\n<li><strong>Tell the therapist about pregnancy, injuries or skin conditions.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Keep the hour after free:</strong> no scooter rush, no heavy dinner.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Book your massage in Ubud</h2>\n<p>THE FACES Ubud, Jl. Raya Lungsiakan, Kedewatan, Ubud, Bali 80571. Open every day, 10:00–22:00. You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or write to us on <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WhatsApp</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li><li><a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">Face massage in Bali: which technique to choose</a></li><li><a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">Head spa in Bali: hair spa, Shirodhara and scalp detox</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 9 min read", "img": "g04-interior.webp", "seo_title": "Massage in Ubud 2026: Types, Prices & Best Treatments | THE FACES Ubud", "metadesc": "Every type of massage in Ubud explained: Balinese, full body, fire, foot reflexology, lymphatic and face massage. Real prices, durations and booking tips.", "faq": [["How much is a massage in Ubud?", "At THE FACES Ubud a full body massage costs IDR 650,000 for 60 minutes, IDR 900,000 for 90 minutes and IDR 950,000 for 120 minutes. Reflexology starts at IDR 300,000 for 30 minutes."], ["Which massage is best after hiking Mount Batur?", "A 90-minute full body massage or the Fire Massage, combined with a leg massage, is ideal after a volcano hike or long walks."], ["How long should a massage be?", "60 minutes is enough for a relaxing massage. Choose 90 or 120 minutes if you have muscle tension or want time for the back, legs and neck."], ["Is THE FACES Ubud open in the evening?", "Yes, THE FACES Ubud is open every day until 22:00, so you can book a massage after dinner."]]}, {"slug": "balinese-massage-guide", "title": "Balinese Massage: What It Is, Benefits and What to Expect", "excerpt": "Everything about Balinese massage: where it comes from, how it works, its benefits, how it compares with Thai and Swedish massage and how to prepare.", "html": "<p>Balinese massage is one of the reasons people fall in love with Bali. It is firm and deeply relaxing at the same time, and it reflects the Balinese idea of balance between body, mind and spirit. Whether you are about to book your first massage on the island or want to understand what makes it special, this guide explains everything you need to know.</p>\n<h2>A short history of Balinese massage</h2>\n<p>Traditional healing in Bali, often called <em>usada</em>, has been practised for centuries by healers known as <em>balian</em>. Over time, local techniques mixed with influences from India, through Ayurveda, and from China, through acupressure. The result is a massage style that uses pressure on energy points, stretching and aromatic oils from the island's plants. Today it is taught in spas and schools across Bali and is the base of most massages you will receive here.</p>\n<h2>The techniques of a Balinese massage</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Palm and thumb pressure</strong> along the muscles of the back, legs and arms.</li>\n<li><strong>Acupressure</strong> on specific points to release blocked tension.</li>\n<li><strong>Gentle stretches</strong> of the arms, legs and back.</li>\n<li><strong>Long, flowing strokes</strong> with warm oil that connect the whole body.</li>\n<li><strong>Skin rolling and kneading</strong> to improve circulation.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Benefits of Balinese massage</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Muscle relaxation:</strong> it releases tension in the back, neck and shoulders.</li>\n<li><strong>Better circulation:</strong> warmth and pressure help blood and lymph move.</li>\n<li><strong>Stress relief:</strong> the slow rhythm calms the nervous system.</li>\n<li><strong>Better sleep:</strong> many guests sleep deeply the night after a massage.</li>\n<li><strong>Recovery:</strong> perfect after hikes, surf sessions and long travel days.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Massage supports well-being; it is not a medical treatment. If you have a health condition, talk to your doctor first.</p>\n<h2>Balinese, Thai or Swedish massage?</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th></th><th>Balinese</th><th>Thai</th><th>Swedish</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Oil</td><td>Yes, warm oil</td><td>No, done clothed</td><td>Yes</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pressure</td><td>Firm, adapted</td><td>Firm, with body weight</td><td>Light to medium</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Stretches</td><td>Gentle</td><td>Many, intense</td><td>None</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Feeling</td><td>Deep and relaxing</td><td>Energising</td><td>Soft and relaxing</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>What to expect at THE FACES</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Welcome and tea.</strong> You tell the therapist what you need: pressure, areas of tension, injuries.</li>\n<li><strong>Changing.</strong> You receive disposable underwear and a robe. During the massage you are always covered with a towel, except the area being worked on.</li>\n<li><strong>The massage.</strong> Back first, then legs, arms, neck and shoulders. You can ask for more or less pressure at any moment.</li>\n<li><strong>Rest.</strong> A few quiet minutes and water or tea before you leave.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Prices at THE FACES</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Full body massage, 60 min: IDR 650,000</li>\n<li>Full body massage, 90 min: IDR 900,000 in Ubud, IDR 850,000 in Sanur</li>\n<li>Full body massage, 120 min: IDR 950,000</li>\n<li>Fire Massage, 90 min: IDR 1,100,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p>See more on the <a href=\"/body-massage/\">body massage page</a> and in the <a href=\"/menu/\">full menu</a>.</p>\n<h2>How to prepare</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Eat lightly at least an hour and a half before.</li>\n<li>Shower before if you come from the beach or the pool.</li>\n<li>Tell us if you are pregnant, have high blood pressure, varicose veins or recent injuries.</li>\n<li>After the massage, drink water and avoid strong sun and alcohol for a few hours.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>The role of oils in Balinese massage</h2>\n<p>Oil is not a detail in a Balinese massage: it is part of the healing. Traditionally, Balinese therapists used coconut oil infused with local plants and spices such as lemongrass, ginger, frangipani and sandalwood. The oil lets the hands glide in long strokes, warms the muscles and leaves the skin soft after days of sun and salt water. If you have a favourite scent or an allergy, tell your therapist before the massage starts.</p>\n<h2>How the pressure feels</h2>\n<p>A Balinese massage is firmer than a Swedish massage but gentler than a Thai massage. The therapist uses the palms and thumbs to press slowly along the muscles, then releases with long strokes. On tight areas, like the shoulders or the lower back, you may feel a \"good pain\" for a few seconds. It should never be sharp. Communication is part of a good massage: a simple \"softer, please\" or \"stronger here\" helps the therapist give you exactly what you need.</p>\n<h2>Balinese massage and the Balinese way of life</h2>\n<p>In Bali, well-being is connected with balance: between people, nature and the spiritual world, a philosophy known as <em>Tri Hita Karana</em>. You feel it in the way a massage is given: without rush, with respect and with attention to the whole person, not just the sore muscle. That is also the spirit of THE FACES: every treatment includes time before and after, so that the calm stays with you when you leave.</p>\n<h2>How often can you have a Balinese massage?</h2>\n<p>On holiday, a massage every two or three days is perfectly fine and helps the body recover from travel, heat and activity. If you live in Bali, a monthly massage is a good routine, or every two weeks if you train hard or work long hours at a desk. Between massages, drink water, stretch and walk: movement keeps the benefits longer.</p>\n<h2>Book a Balinese massage</h2>\n<p>You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 8 min read", "img": "g05-interior-s.webp", "seo_title": "Balinese Massage: What It Is, Benefits & What to Expect | THE FACES Bali", "metadesc": "What is a Balinese massage? History, techniques, benefits, how it differs from Thai and Swedish massage, what to expect and where to book in Ubud and Sanur.", "faq": [["What is a Balinese massage?", "Balinese massage is the traditional massage of Bali. It combines firm pressure with the palms and thumbs, gentle stretches, acupressure and long strokes with warm oil to release tension and improve circulation."], ["Is Balinese massage painful?", "It should not be painful. The pressure is firm but always adapted to you: tell the therapist if you want it stronger or softer."], ["What is the difference between Balinese and Thai massage?", "Thai massage is done clothed, without oil, with many stretches. Balinese massage uses warm oil on the skin and combines pressure, acupressure and long relaxing strokes."], ["How long should a Balinese massage be?", "60 minutes is good for relaxation, 90 minutes is ideal for a complete treatment of the back, legs, arms, neck and shoulders."]]}, {"slug": "facial-bali-skin-care-guide", "title": "Facial in Bali: The Complete Guide to Skin Care Treatments", "excerpt": "Sun, humidity and sunscreen change your skin in Bali. Here is how to choose the right facial: cleansing, hydration, oxygen, cryomassage and more.", "html": "<p>Bali is wonderful for the soul and a little harder on the skin. Strong sun, humidity, sweat, salt water, chlorine and several layers of sunscreen a day clog pores, dehydrate the surface and make the complexion dull. A professional facial resets the skin so that you leave Bali glowing, not tired. This guide explains the facial treatments at THE FACES and helps you choose the right one.</p>\n<h2>What the tropical climate does to your skin</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Congested pores:</strong> sweat and sunscreen mix and block the pores, especially on the nose and chin.</li>\n<li><strong>Dehydration:</strong> sun and air conditioning take water from the skin, even when it looks oily.</li>\n<li><strong>Dullness and uneven tone:</strong> the surface thickens to protect itself from UV.</li>\n<li><strong>Puffiness:</strong> heat and salty food make the face swell in the morning.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Facial cleansing</h2>\n<p>A professional cleansing removes impurities, opens congested pores and prepares the skin to absorb care. We offer four methods:</p>\n<h3>Atraumatic facial cleansing · 110 min · IDR 1,200,000</h3>\n<p>A gentle method that cleans deeply without aggressive extraction, so the skin does not stay red for days. Ideal for sensitive skin and for a first cleansing.</p>\n<h3>Vacuum facial cleansing · 120 min · IDR 1,200,000</h3>\n<p>A soft vacuum lifts impurities from the pores. Great for combination skin with blackheads.</p>\n<h3>Ultrasonic facial cleansing · 120 min · IDR 1,200,000</h3>\n<p>Ultrasonic vibrations exfoliate and clean without friction. A good choice for a fresh, even surface.</p>\n<h3>Combination facial cleansing · 150 min · IDR 1,350,000</h3>\n<p>Several methods in one session, for skin that needs a full reset.</p>\n<h2>Hydration and glow</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Deep skin hydration</strong>, 80 min, IDR 1,000,000: the best answer to sun and air conditioning.</li>\n<li><strong>Oxygen pen</strong>, 75 min, IDR 900,000: oxygen and active care for a fresh, radiant complexion.</li>\n<li><strong>Cryomassage</strong>, 75 min, IDR 970,000: cold tightens pores, reduces puffiness and tones the skin.</li>\n<li><strong>Lymphatic Glow</strong>, 90 min, IDR 1,000,000 (Ubud): lymphatic drainage of the face for a de-puffed, luminous result.</li>\n<li><strong>Hydrolift</strong>, 60 min, IDR 850,000 (Sanur): intensive hydration with a lifting effect.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How to choose your facial</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Your skin</th><th>Our recommendation</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Sensitive, first facial</td><td>Atraumatic cleansing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Blackheads, combination skin</td><td>Vacuum or combination cleansing</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Dehydrated after the sun</td><td>Deep skin hydration</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Dull, tired</td><td>Oxygen pen</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Puffy in the morning</td><td>Cryomassage or Lymphatic Glow</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Before an event</td><td>Hydrolift + face massage (Sanur)</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Facial and face massage: the perfect pair</h2>\n<p>A facial cares for the surface of the skin; a face massage works on the muscles and the fascia underneath. Together they give the best result: clean, hydrated skin and a lifted contour. Book them on two different days, or ask for a combined plan. Read our <a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">face massage guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Before and after your facial</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Avoid sunbathing the day before and the day after a cleansing.</li>\n<li>Come without make-up if you can.</li>\n<li>Tell us about retinoids, acids, recent peels or injections.</li>\n<li>Use a high SPF sunscreen and a light moisturiser for the following days.</li>\n<li>Do not swim in the sea or the pool on the day of a cleansing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Plan a skin routine for your holiday</h2>\n<p>For a two-week stay, many guests book a cleansing at the start, a hydration in the middle and a face massage before flying home. Your skin is clean, hydrated and lifted for the photos and for the return.</p>\n<h2>Building a simple skin routine in Bali</h2>\n<p>Between professional treatments, a simple routine keeps the skin balanced in the tropical climate:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Morning:</strong> a gentle cleanser, a light hydrating serum and a high SPF sunscreen, reapplied after swimming and every two hours in the sun.</li>\n<li><strong>Evening:</strong> a double cleanse to remove sunscreen and sweat, then a light moisturiser. Heavy creams can feel suffocating in the humidity.</li>\n<li><strong>Once or twice a week:</strong> a gentle exfoliation or a hydrating mask, never on sunburnt skin.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Sunburn and sensitive skin</h2>\n<p>If your face is sunburnt, postpone cleansings, peeling-type treatments and cryomassage. Choose deep hydration or a gentle Lymphatic Glow once the redness has calmed down, and tell the therapist. For very sensitive or reactive skin, the atraumatic cleansing is the safest first step.</p>\n<h2>How long do the results last?</h2>\n<p>A cleansing keeps the pores clear for two to four weeks, depending on your skin and on how much sunscreen and sweat it receives. Hydration and oxygen treatments give an immediate glow that lasts several days and builds up with regular sessions. For the best long-term result, alternate a cleansing every month with a hydrating treatment and a face massage.</p>\n<h2>Facials for men</h2>\n<p>Men's skin is thicker and often oilier, and shaving adds irritation. A vacuum or ultrasonic cleansing clears the pores, while deep hydration calms the skin after shaving and sun. Many men combine a facial with a myofascial facial massage to release jaw tension.</p>\n<h2>Book your facial</h2>\n<p>More details on the <a href=\"/skin-care/\">skin care page</a>. You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or ask us on WhatsApp which facial suits your skin: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">Face massage in Bali: which technique to choose</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "face", "cat": "Face · 9 min read", "img": "g02-face-s.webp", "seo_title": "Facial in Bali: Cleansing, Hydration, Oxygen & Cryo Prices | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Which facial to choose in Bali? Atraumatic, vacuum, ultrasonic and combination cleansing, deep hydration, oxygen pen, cryomassage and Lymphatic Glow, with prices.", "faq": [["What is the best facial in Bali for sun-damaged skin?", "Deep skin hydration (80 min, IDR 1,000,000) is the best choice after days of sun. Combine it with a gentle atraumatic cleansing if your pores feel congested."], ["How much is a facial at THE FACES?", "Facial cleansings cost IDR 1,200,000 (atraumatic, vacuum or ultrasonic) or IDR 1,350,000 (combination). Deep hydration is IDR 1,000,000, the oxygen pen IDR 900,000 and cryomassage IDR 970,000."], ["Can I go in the sun after a facial?", "Avoid strong sun for the rest of the day, especially after a cleansing, and use a high SPF sunscreen for the next days."], ["Is a facial cleansing painful?", "Our atraumatic cleansing is designed to be gentle. Vacuum and ultrasonic cleansings are also comfortable; the therapist adapts the intensity to your skin."]]}, {"slug": "lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali", "title": "Lymphatic Drainage Massage in Bali: Benefits, Prices and When to Book", "excerpt": "Heavy legs after the flight? Puffy face in the heat? How lymphatic drainage works, its benefits and the best treatments for legs and face in Bali.", "html": "<p>Long-haul flights, heat, humidity, salty food and cocktails by the pool: it is no surprise that many travellers in Bali wake up with heavy legs and a puffy face. Lymphatic drainage massage is one of the most effective ways to feel light again. Here is how it works, what it does and which treatment to choose at THE FACES.</p>\n<h2>What is the lymphatic system?</h2>\n<p>The lymphatic system is a network of vessels and nodes that carries fluid, called lymph, back towards the blood and helps the body eliminate waste. Unlike blood, lymph has no pump: it moves thanks to muscle movement and breathing. When we sit for hours on a plane or stay still in the heat, it slows down, and fluid accumulates in the legs and the face.</p>\n<h2>How lymphatic drainage massage works</h2>\n<p>The therapist uses light, slow, rhythmic movements that follow the direction of the lymphatic vessels towards the lymph nodes. The pressure is much softer than in a classic massage: the goal is not to work on the muscles, but to help the fluid move. Many guests find it surprisingly relaxing.</p>\n<h2>Benefits</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lighter legs</strong> after a long flight or a day on your feet.</li>\n<li><strong>Less puffiness</strong> in the face and around the eyes.</li>\n<li><strong>A defined contour</strong> of the face and the ankles.</li>\n<li><strong>Deep relaxation</strong> thanks to the slow rhythm.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Lymphatic treatments at THE FACES</h2>\n<h3>Lymphatic drainage / relaxing leg massage</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>30 min: IDR 300,000</li>\n<li>60 min: IDR 500,000</li>\n<li>90 min: IDR 600,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Available in Ubud and Sanur. The 60-minute version is the most booked on arrival day.</p>\n<h3>Lymphatic Glow · 90 min · IDR 1,000,000 · Ubud</h3>\n<p>Lymphatic drainage for the face: it reduces puffiness, defines the contour and gives a luminous complexion. Perfect the morning before an event.</p>\n<h3>Gua sha massage · 60 min · IDR 750,000</h3>\n<p>The traditional stone tool also drains the face beautifully.</p>\n<h3>Before Flight Ritual · IDR 2,200,000</h3>\n<p>Our ritual for the last day of your trip includes care for the legs, the head and the face, so that you fly relaxed and land less swollen.</p>\n<h2>When to book lymphatic drainage in Bali</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The day you arrive</strong> or the day after, to recover from the flight.</li>\n<li><strong>After days of heat</strong> when the ankles start to swell.</li>\n<li><strong>The morning of an event</strong>, for a de-puffed face.</li>\n<li><strong>Before flying home</strong>, to prepare the legs for the flight.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Who should ask a doctor first</h2>\n<p>Lymphatic drainage is gentle, but it is not suitable for everyone. If you have or had thrombosis, an acute infection, a heart or kidney condition, cancer treatment or if you are pregnant, consult your doctor first and tell the therapist before the session.</p>\n<h2>Tips to support your lymph on holiday</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Drink plenty of water, especially with alcohol and in the heat.</li>\n<li>Walk and swim: muscle movement moves the lymph.</li>\n<li>Raise your legs for ten minutes in the evening.</li>\n<li>Limit very salty food.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Lymphatic drainage vs a classic massage</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th></th><th>Lymphatic drainage</th><th>Classic massage</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Pressure</td><td>Very light</td><td>Medium to firm</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Goal</td><td>Move fluid, reduce swelling</td><td>Release muscle tension</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Rhythm</td><td>Slow, repetitive, towards the lymph nodes</td><td>Varied</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Best for</td><td>Heavy legs, puffiness, after flights</td><td>Sore muscles, stress</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>What to expect during your session</h2>\n<p>You lie comfortably on the treatment bed, usually with the legs slightly raised. The therapist starts near the lymph nodes, for example behind the knees and at the top of the thighs, to \"open the way\", then works from the feet upwards with slow, light, rhythmic movements. Many guests feel the legs become lighter during the session. After the treatment you may need to use the bathroom more often: it is a sign that the body is releasing fluid.</p>\n<h2>How many sessions?</h2>\n<p>One session after a flight is enough to feel the difference. If your legs often swell in the heat, two or three sessions during your holiday, a few days apart, give a longer-lasting result. Combine them with walking, swimming and plenty of water.</p>\n<h2>Lymphatic drainage for the face</h2>\n<p>The face also holds fluid, especially around the eyes and the jawline after salty food, alcohol or a short night. Facial lymphatic drainage uses the same light movements, directed towards the lymph nodes of the neck. The result is a fresher, more defined face, which is why many guests book Lymphatic Glow or gua sha on the morning of a wedding, a party or a photo shoot.</p>\n<h2>Book your lymphatic drainage</h2>\n<p>You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>. See all body treatments on the <a href=\"/body-massage/\">body massage page</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/facial-bali-skin-care-guide/\">Facial in Bali: the complete skin care guide</a></li><li><a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">Face massage in Bali: which technique to choose</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 7 min read", "img": "g09-proc-s.webp", "seo_title": "Lymphatic Drainage Massage Bali: Benefits & Prices | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali for swollen legs, jet lag and a de-puffed face. How it works, benefits, legs and face treatments, prices in Ubud and Sanur.", "faq": [["What is lymphatic drainage massage?", "It is a gentle, rhythmic massage that follows the direction of the lymphatic system to help the body release excess fluid. It reduces the feeling of heavy, swollen legs and a puffy face."], ["Is lymphatic drainage good after a long flight?", "Yes. After a long flight the legs often feel heavy and swollen. A 60-minute lymphatic drainage leg massage is one of the most popular treatments for arrival day."], ["How much is lymphatic drainage at THE FACES?", "The lymphatic drainage / relaxing leg massage costs IDR 300,000 for 30 minutes, IDR 500,000 for 60 minutes and IDR 600,000 for 90 minutes. Lymphatic Glow for the face is IDR 1,000,000 (90 min, Ubud)."], ["Who should avoid lymphatic drainage?", "People with thrombosis, acute infections, heart or kidney conditions or who are pregnant should consult a doctor first and tell the therapist before the treatment."]]}, {"slug": "foot-reflexology-bali", "title": "Foot Reflexology in Bali: What It Is and Why Travellers Love It", "excerpt": "After the rice terraces, the temples and the beach path, your feet deserve care. How foot reflexology works and which session to book.", "html": "<p>In Bali you walk more than you think: up and down the steps of temples, along the rice terraces, on the beach path in Sanur and through the streets of Ubud in sandals. By the end of the day the feet are tired and the legs heavy. Foot reflexology is the simplest way to recover, and one of the most relaxing treatments on our menu.</p>\n<h2>What is reflexology?</h2>\n<p>Reflexology is a massage technique based on the idea that points on the feet correspond to areas of the body. The therapist applies precise pressure with the thumbs and fingers, combined with relaxing strokes of the feet, the ankles and the lower legs. Whatever you think of the theory, the effect is easy to feel: the feet relax, the legs feel lighter and the whole body calms down.</p>\n<h2>Benefits travellers notice</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Relief for tired, sore feet after long walks.</li>\n<li>Lighter legs after a flight or a day in the heat.</li>\n<li>Deep relaxation, often with sleep during the session.</li>\n<li>A gentle treatment that suits almost everyone, including older guests.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Reflexology at THE FACES</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reflexology foot massage, 30 min: IDR 300,000</li>\n<li>Reflexology foot massage, 60 min: IDR 500,000</li>\n<li>Reflexology foot massage, 90 min: IDR 600,000</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In Sanur, try <strong>4 hands</strong> (IDR 950,000): a face massage and foot reflexology at the same time, with two therapists. It is one of the most relaxing experiences you can have in Bali.</p>\n<h2>How to use reflexology in your trip</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>After a day of sightseeing:</strong> 60 minutes in the evening, Ubud is open until 22:00.</li>\n<li><strong>As an add-on:</strong> 30 minutes after a face massage or a head spa.</li>\n<li><strong>For the whole family:</strong> grandparents and parents can enjoy it side by side.</li>\n<li><strong>After the beach path in Sanur:</strong> walk from the beach to our salon on Jl. Danau Buyan.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What to expect</h2>\n<p>You sit comfortably in a reclining chair or lie on the treatment bed. The therapist cleans your feet with warm water, then works with oil or balm on the feet, the ankles and the calves. You can tell the therapist at any moment if the pressure is too strong. Some points may feel tender: that is normal and passes quickly.</p>\n<h2>Who should ask first</h2>\n<p>Tell us if you are pregnant, have diabetes with reduced sensation in the feet, open wounds, fungal infections or recent injuries. The therapist will adapt the treatment or suggest another one.</p>\n<h2>A short history of reflexology</h2>\n<p>Working on the feet to relax the whole body is an ancient practice found in Chinese, Egyptian and Indian traditions. Modern reflexology was developed in the twentieth century, with maps that link areas of the feet to organs and systems of the body. In Bali, foot massage is a natural partner of the island's walking culture: temples, rice fields and beaches are best explored on foot.</p>\n<h2>Reflexology vs a simple foot massage</h2>\n<p>A foot massage relaxes the feet with strokes and kneading. Reflexology adds precise, sustained pressure on specific points, following a sequence across the whole sole, the heels, the toes and the ankles. The result is deeper: many guests feel the effect in the legs, the back and even the mind, and fall asleep during the session.</p>\n<h2>Which duration to choose</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>30 minutes:</strong> a quick reset after a walk or as an add-on to another treatment.</li>\n<li><strong>60 minutes:</strong> a complete session for feet, ankles and calves. Our most popular choice.</li>\n<li><strong>90 minutes:</strong> a long, deep treatment that includes the lower legs, perfect after hikes or long flights.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Reflexology for the whole family</h2>\n<p>Reflexology is gentle, done in a comfortable position and does not require undressing, which makes it ideal for older guests, for people who are shy about full body massage and for the whole family. Book side by side sessions so that everyone finishes together.</p>\n<h2>After your session</h2>\n<p>Drink water, keep your feet warm and avoid long walks for the next hour. Many guests notice that they sleep better the night after a reflexology session.</p>\n<h2>Book your reflexology</h2>\n<p>You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 6 min read", "img": "g12-proc-s.webp", "seo_title": "Foot Reflexology Bali: Benefits, Prices & Where to Book | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Foot reflexology in Bali after long walks, hikes and flights. What reflexology is, benefits, 30, 60 and 90-minute sessions and prices in Ubud and Sanur.", "faq": [["What is foot reflexology?", "Foot reflexology is a massage technique that applies pressure to specific points on the feet. In reflexology each point is linked to an area of the body. It is deeply relaxing and relieves tired feet and legs."], ["How long is a reflexology session?", "At THE FACES you can choose 30, 60 or 90 minutes. 30 minutes is perfect as an add-on, 60 minutes as a complete treatment."], ["How much is foot reflexology in Bali?", "At THE FACES reflexology costs IDR 300,000 for 30 minutes, IDR 500,000 for 60 minutes and IDR 600,000 for 90 minutes."], ["Can I combine reflexology with a face massage?", "Yes. In Sanur the 4 hands treatment combines a face massage and foot reflexology at the same time, with two therapists (IDR 950,000)."]]}, {"slug": "mens-spa-bali", "title": "Spa for Men in Bali: Treatments Designed for Men", "excerpt": "More and more men book spa treatments in Bali. The programmes designed for men at THE FACES, and the treatments men choose most.", "html": "<p>Spa is no longer just for women, and in Bali more and more men book massages, head spas and even face treatments. Whether you are recovering from surf sessions, long scooter rides, a Mount Batur hike or simply work stress, here is what THE FACES offers for men and how to choose.</p>\n<h2>Why men book spa treatments in Bali</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Physical recovery:</strong> surf, hikes, gym and long rides leave sore muscles.</li>\n<li><strong>Stress:</strong> many guests come to Bali to switch off from demanding jobs.</li>\n<li><strong>Sleep and jet lag:</strong> a deep massage or head spa resets the body clock.</li>\n<li><strong>Looking fresh:</strong> before a wedding, a meeting or a photo shoot.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Programmes designed for men (Ubud)</h2>\n<h3>Power Reset · 130 min · IDR 1,400,000</h3>\n<p>A programme to recover energy: deep work on the back, shoulders and legs, where men hold most tension, combined with treatments that restore focus.</p>\n<h3>Stress Free · 120 min · IDR 2,100,000</h3>\n<p>A complete reset for the nervous system, for men who arrive in Bali exhausted and want to switch off fast.</p>\n<h2>The treatments men choose most</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fire Massage</strong>, 90 min, IDR 1,100,000: warmth and deep pressure for tight muscles.</li>\n<li><strong>Full body massage</strong>, 60 / 90 / 120 min: IDR 650,000 / 900,000 (850,000 in Sanur) / 950,000.</li>\n<li><strong>Reflexology</strong>, 30 / 60 / 90 min: IDR 300,000 / 500,000 / 600,000.</li>\n<li><strong>Water spa therapy with detox hair spa</strong>, 90 min, IDR 1,100,000: the head spa men end up loving.</li>\n<li><strong>Myofascial facial massage</strong>, 90 min, IDR 900,000: for jaw clenching and screen fatigue.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Face massage for men: why it works</h2>\n<p>Men clench their jaw more than they think, especially under stress or during sport. Tension in the jaw, the temples and the neck causes headaches and a tired face. A myofascial facial massage releases it in one session. Read our <a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">face massage guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Practical tips for men</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No need to shave before a face massage, but tell the therapist if your skin is irritated.</li>\n<li>Ask for stronger pressure if you are used to deep massage, or softer if you are sunburnt.</li>\n<li>After surf, wait until the skin has cooled down and shower before your massage.</li>\n<li>Book in the evening: Ubud is open until 22:00.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Recovery after surf, hikes and gym</h2>\n<p>Bali is an active island. Surfing paddles the shoulders and the upper back, a Mount Batur sunrise hike loads the legs and the knees, and long scooter rides stiffen the neck and the lower back. A deep massage within a day or two of the effort helps the muscles recover. Book the Fire Massage for overall tension, add 30 minutes of reflexology for the legs and feet, and finish with a head massage if you have been squinting in the sun all day.</p>\n<h2>Stress and burnout</h2>\n<p>Many of our male guests come to Bali to recover from intense work periods. The body often shows it before the mind: a tight jaw, shoulders up to the ears, shallow breathing and poor sleep. A combination of deep massage and head spa, or the Stress Free programme, works on both levels. The Shirodhara Hair Spa is another strong choice for an overloaded mind.</p>\n<h2>Grooming before a big day</h2>\n<p>Getting married in Bali, attending a wedding, or flying home to an important meeting? Book a facial cleansing two or three days before, and a myofascial facial massage the day before. The skin is clear, the face relaxed and the contour defined, without looking \"treated\".</p>\n<h2>What men often ask us</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Do I need to undress completely?</strong> No. You receive disposable underwear and you are always covered with a towel.</li>\n<li><strong>Can I ask for a male therapist?</strong> Ask the team when you book; we will do our best to accommodate your preference.</li>\n<li><strong>Will a face massage make me look different?</strong> It makes you look rested, not different.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Book your treatment</h2>\n<p>You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">Head spa in Bali: hair spa, Shirodhara and scalp detox</a></li><li><a href=\"/face-massage-bali-guide/\">Face massage in Bali: which technique to choose</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "rituals", "cat": "Rituals · 6 min read", "img": "g11-proc-s.webp", "seo_title": "Men's Spa Bali: Massage & Treatments for Men | THE FACES Ubud", "metadesc": "Spa treatments for men in Bali: Power Reset and Stress Free programmes, deep massage, head spa and face massage for men. Prices and tips in Ubud and Sanur.", "faq": [["Do you have spa treatments for men?", "Yes. In Ubud we offer two programmes designed for men: Power Reset (130 min, IDR 1,400,000) and Stress Free (120 min, IDR 2,100,000). All our massages, head spa and face treatments are also available for men."], ["What is the best massage for men after surfing?", "The Fire Massage (90 min, IDR 1,100,000) or a 90-minute full body massage, combined with a reflexology session for the legs and feet."], ["Is face massage for men too?", "Absolutely. Many men book the myofascial facial massage for jaw tension, screen fatigue and a fresher face before meetings or events."], ["Can I book with my partner?", "Yes, you can book side by side treatments or one of our couples rituals."]]}, {"slug": "things-to-do-in-sanur", "title": "Things to Do in Sanur: A Slow Guide to Bali's Calm Coast", "excerpt": "Sanur is Bali at a slower pace. Sunrise walks, cycling, island day trips, local food and a spa afternoon: our guide to the calm coast.", "html": "<p>Sanur is the Bali that many people dream of before they arrive: palm trees over a calm sea, a long path along the beach, sunrise every morning and a relaxed, friendly pace. It is less crowded than Seminyak or Canggu and perfect for families, couples and anyone who wants to rest. Here is our slow guide to the best things to do in Sanur, written by the team of THE FACES Sanur.</p>\n<h2>1. Watch the sunrise on the beach</h2>\n<p>Sanur faces east, so the sunrise over the sea is the main event of the day. Be on the beach before 6:00 on clear mornings, with a coffee, and watch the fishing boats and Mount Agung on very clear days.</p>\n<h2>2. Walk or cycle the beach path</h2>\n<p>A long paved path runs along the seafront, past hotels, warungs, temples and small beaches. Walk it in the early morning, or rent a bicycle and ride from end to end. It is the best way to discover Sanur's different beaches.</p>\n<h2>3. Swim in calm water</h2>\n<p>A reef protects much of Sanur's coast, so the water is usually calm and shallow at high tide: ideal for children and for a relaxed swim. Check the tide, because at low tide the water can be very shallow.</p>\n<h2>4. Take a day trip to Nusa Lembongan or Nusa Penida</h2>\n<p>Fast boats to the Nusa islands leave from Sanur. Spend a day snorkelling with manta rays, visiting the famous viewpoints of Nusa Penida or relaxing on the white beaches of Lembongan. Book with a reputable operator and check the sea conditions.</p>\n<h2>5. Try snorkelling, paddleboard or kitesurf</h2>\n<p>The calm lagoon is great for stand-up paddle and beginner snorkelling, and some seasons bring good wind for kitesurfing on the southern beaches.</p>\n<h2>6. Eat at the night market and local warungs</h2>\n<p>In the evening, look for the local night market and the small warungs where Balinese families eat: satay, nasi campur, grilled fish and fresh juices at local prices.</p>\n<h2>7. Discover art and history</h2>\n<p>Sanur has a long artistic history. Visit the museum dedicated to the Belgian painter Le Mayeur, who lived and painted by the beach, and look for the small temples hidden along the path.</p>\n<h2>8. Spend an afternoon at the spa</h2>\n<p>After a morning of sea and sun, the afternoon is perfect for a spa. At <a href=\"/sanur/\">THE FACES Sanur</a>, on Jl. Danau Buyan, a few minutes from the beach, guests choose:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Myofascial facial massage</strong>, 90 min, IDR 900,000</li>\n<li><strong>Hydrolift</strong>, 60 min, IDR 850,000, ideal for skin tired by sun and sea</li>\n<li><strong>Airkiss Detox Ritual</strong>, 60 min, IDR 1,300,000</li>\n<li><strong>Foamy Dream Ritual</strong>, 120 min, IDR 2,300,000</li>\n<li><strong>Reflexology</strong>, 30 / 60 / 90 min, after the beach walk</li>\n<li><strong>Sacred Honeymoon ritual</strong>, 200 min, IDR 3,800,000, for couples</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Read our complete <a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">guide to the spa in Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>9. Use Sanur as your last stop before the airport</h2>\n<p>Sanur is close to the airport, so it is the perfect place for the last night of your trip. On departure day, book our Before Flight Ritual (IDR 2,200,000): care for the legs, head and face so that you board relaxed.</p>\n<h2>A perfect day in Sanur</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Sunrise on the beach and breakfast by the sea.</li>\n<li>Bike ride along the beach path.</li>\n<li>Swim at high tide and lunch at a warung.</li>\n<li>Spa afternoon at THE FACES Sanur.</li>\n<li>Sunset drinks and dinner at the night market.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>When to visit Sanur</h2>\n<p>The dry season, roughly April to October, brings sunny days and calm evenings. The rainy season, roughly November to March, is greener and quieter, with short tropical showers: perfect weather for a spa afternoon.</p>\n<h2>Sanur with children</h2>\n<p>Sanur is one of the most family-friendly areas of Bali. The calm water inside the reef, the flat beach path for strollers and bicycles, and the relaxed beachfront restaurants make it easy to travel with children. Plan beach time around the tides, take shade breaks in the middle of the day and keep the afternoons for the pool or a nap.</p>\n<h2>Where to stay in Sanur</h2>\n<p>The beachfront between the north and south ends of Sanur offers hotels and villas with direct access to the path. Staying a few streets back is quieter and more affordable, and everything remains within walking or cycling distance. Our salon on Jl. Danau Buyan is in this calm residential area, a few minutes from the beach.</p>\n<h2>Getting around</h2>\n<p>Sanur is flat and compact. Walk or cycle along the beach path, and use Grab or Gojek for longer distances. From Sanur, Ubud is around an hour away by car, depending on traffic, which makes day trips to the rice terraces and temples easy.</p>\n<h2>Combine Sanur and Ubud</h2>\n<p>Many travellers split their stay between the jungle and the sea: a few nights in Ubud for the rice fields, the temples and the culture, then a few nights in Sanur to rest by the sea before flying home. THE FACES has a salon in both, so you can start a course of treatments in one and continue in the other. Read our guide to the <a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">best spa in Ubud</a>.</p>\n<h2>Rainy day ideas in Sanur</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A long spa afternoon: head spa, face massage or a foam ritual.</li>\n<li>A Balinese cooking class.</li>\n<li>Coffee and a book in one of the cafés along the path.</li>\n<li>Art galleries and small boutiques.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Book your spa in Sanur</h2>\n<p>THE FACES Sanur, Jl. Danau Buyan No. 34a, Sanur, Denpasar Selatan, Bali 80227. Open every day, 10:00–20:00. You can <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a> or write to us on <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WhatsApp</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/couples-spa-bali-honeymoon/\">Couples spa in Bali: rituals for two</a></li><li><a href=\"/lymphatic-drainage-massage-bali/\">Lymphatic drainage massage in Bali</a></li><li><a href=\"/facial-bali-skin-care-guide/\">Facial in Bali: the complete skin care guide</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "news", "cat": "Guides · 9 min read", "img": "salon-sanur.jpg", "seo_title": "Things to Do in Sanur 2026: Beach, Sunrise, Food & Spa | THE FACES", "metadesc": "The best things to do in Sanur, Bali: sunrise on the beach path, cycling, snorkelling, day trips to Nusa Lembongan and Penida, night market, and a spa day.", "faq": [["Is Sanur worth visiting?", "Yes. Sanur is calm, family-friendly and close to the airport, with a long beach path, sunrise views and easy boat trips to Nusa Lembongan and Nusa Penida."], ["What is Sanur best known for?", "Sanur is known for its sunrise, its long seafront path along the beach, calm water protected by the reef and its relaxed atmosphere."], ["How far is Sanur from the airport?", "The drive from Ngurah Rai airport to Sanur usually takes around 30 minutes, depending on traffic."], ["Where can I get a spa treatment in Sanur?", "THE FACES Sanur is at Jl. Danau Buyan No. 34a, open every day from 10:00 to 20:00, with face massage, head spa, foam rituals and couples treatments."]]}, {"slug": "shirodhara-bali-ayurveda", "title": "Shirodhara in Bali: The Ayurvedic Oil Ritual for Deep Calm", "excerpt": "A thin stream of warm oil on the forehead, and the mind goes quiet. What Shirodhara is, what it feels like and how we combine it with a hair spa.", "html": "<p>Some treatments relax the body. Shirodhara quiets the mind. A thin, warm stream of oil flows slowly over the forehead, and within minutes most guests feel their thoughts slow down. It is one of the oldest rituals of Ayurveda and one of the most memorable treatments you can experience in Bali.</p>\n<h2>What is Shirodhara?</h2>\n<p>The name comes from Sanskrit: <em>shiro</em>, head, and <em>dhara</em>, flow. The guest lies on their back while warm oil is poured in a continuous stream onto the forehead, the point that Ayurveda calls the third eye. The stream moves gently from side to side. The sensation is warm, rhythmic and hypnotic.</p>\n<h2>Why it feels so calming</h2>\n<p>The steady warmth and rhythm give the mind one simple thing to follow, which is why many guests drift into a state between waking and sleep. In Ayurveda, Shirodhara is used to calm an overactive mind and to support sleep. Modern guests often describe it as the deepest relaxation they have ever felt.</p>\n<h2>Who Shirodhara is for</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>People who arrive in Bali exhausted and cannot switch off.</li>\n<li>Travellers with jet lag and disturbed sleep.</li>\n<li>Anyone with a busy mind who struggles to meditate.</li>\n<li>Guests looking for a unique, memorable ritual.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>The Shirodhara Hair Spa at THE FACES · 120 min · IDR 1,650,000</h2>\n<p>We combine the classic Shirodhara with a full hair spa, so that the ritual cares for both the mind and the hair:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Welcome</strong>, tea and a short conversation about your needs.</li>\n<li><strong>Head, neck and shoulder massage</strong> to prepare the body.</li>\n<li><strong>Shirodhara:</strong> the warm oil stream on the forehead.</li>\n<li><strong>Hair spa:</strong> cleansing, nourishing care and warm water therapy for the scalp.</li>\n<li><strong>Rest</strong> before you leave.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Other Ayurvedic and head treatments</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ayurvedic head massage</strong>, 60 min, IDR 750,000: the short version, with warm oil.</li>\n<li><strong>Water spa therapy with detox hair spa</strong>, 90 min, IDR 1,100,000.</li>\n<li><strong>Hair spa &amp; water detox + face massage</strong>, 120 min, IDR 1,500,000.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Compare them in our <a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">head spa guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>Before and after Shirodhara</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Plan nothing demanding afterwards: the calm lasts for hours.</li>\n<li>Do not drive a scooter immediately after; take a car or rest first.</li>\n<li>Keep your hair simple for the rest of the day.</li>\n<li>Drink warm water or tea and go to bed early: the night after is often the best sleep of the trip.</li>\n<li>Tell us if you are pregnant, have a scalp condition, a cold or high blood pressure.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>A short introduction to Ayurveda</h2>\n<p>Ayurveda, the \"science of life\", is a traditional system of well-being from India that is thousands of years old. It sees health as a balance between body, mind and environment, and uses diet, herbs, oils, massage and daily routines to restore it. Its influence reached Bali centuries ago, and you can still feel it in the island's healing traditions and in the warm oils used in Balinese massage.</p>\n<h2>The oil used in Shirodhara</h2>\n<p>Traditionally, Shirodhara is performed with warm herbal oils or sesame oil, chosen according to the person's constitution. The oil is warmed to body temperature, so the stream feels comforting rather than hot or cold. If you have allergies or sensitive skin, tell us before the ritual and we will adapt the oil.</p>\n<h2>What it feels like, minute by minute</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The first minutes:</strong> warmth on the forehead, a light tickle, the mind still busy.</li>\n<li><strong>After five to ten minutes:</strong> breathing slows, the face relaxes and thoughts become distant.</li>\n<li><strong>The heart of the ritual:</strong> many guests enter a dreamy state between waking and sleeping.</li>\n<li><strong>The end:</strong> a feeling of lightness and calm that lasts for the rest of the day.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How often can you do Shirodhara?</h2>\n<p>As a holiday experience, one session is enough to remember it for a long time. People who live in Bali and use it as a stress reset often book it once a month. In traditional Ayurveda it can be part of a series of sessions over several days, guided by a practitioner.</p>\n<h2>Shirodhara and sleep</h2>\n<p>Many guests tell us that the night after Shirodhara is the best sleep of their trip. To make the most of it, have a light dinner, avoid screens in the evening and go to bed early.</p>\n<h2>Book your Shirodhara</h2>\n<p>You can <a href=\"https://n831884.alteg.io/company/780725/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Ubud</a> or <a href=\"https://n811764.alteg.io/company/762669/personal/select-services?o=m-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">book online in Sanur</a>, or write to us on WhatsApp: <a href=\"https://wa.me/6282266999965\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ubud</a>, <a href=\"https://wa.me/6281337709190\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sanur</a>.</p>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/head-spa-bali-guide/\">Head spa in Bali: hair spa, Shirodhara and scalp detox</a></li><li><a href=\"/massage-in-ubud-guide/\">Massage in Ubud: types, prices and tips</a></li><li><a href=\"/best-spa-in-ubud-guide/\">Best spa in Ubud: how to choose your treatment</a></li><li><a href=\"/spa-in-sanur-guide/\">Spa in Sanur: treatments, prices and tips</a></li></ul>", "catkey": "head", "cat": "Head spa · 7 min read", "img": "g10-proc-s.webp", "seo_title": "Shirodhara Bali: Ayurvedic Oil Ritual, Benefits & Price | THE FACES", "metadesc": "Shirodhara in Bali: the Ayurvedic ritual of warm oil on the forehead for stress, sleep and an overloaded mind. What happens, benefits and the Shirodhara Hair Spa.", "faq": [["What is Shirodhara?", "Shirodhara is an Ayurvedic treatment in which a thin, continuous stream of warm oil flows over the forehead. It is known for its deeply calming effect on the mind."], ["What are the benefits of Shirodhara?", "Guests describe deep relaxation, a quiet mind and better sleep. In Ayurveda it is used to calm stress and an overactive mind. It is a well-being treatment, not a medical one."], ["How much is Shirodhara at THE FACES?", "The Shirodhara Hair Spa lasts 120 minutes and costs IDR 1,650,000."], ["Will my hair be oily after Shirodhara?", "The oil is part of the treatment. We wash the hair at the end, but it is best to keep the hair simple for the rest of the day and wash it again the next day."]]}]
